## Architectural Decisions

**Why event time over processing time?**
Event time ensures every price tick is assigned to the window when the price actually occurred. Processing time windowing would silently assign late messages to wrong windows.

**Why fixed AND sliding windows?**
Fixed windows (5-min) answer "what is the price right now?" Sliding windows (1-hr/15-min) answer "what is the typical price?" Both needed for anomaly detection.

**Why BigQuery Silver has duplicates?**
BigQuery streaming inserts are append-only. Dataflow's accumulating mode fires a window result twice. Deduplication happens in Spark using ROW_NUMBER() window function.

**Why two layers (Silver + Gold)?**
Silver is raw and immutable — full history, used for reprocessing. Gold is clean and analytical — deduplicated, dimensional, optimized for queries.

**Why SCD Type 2 for dim_flights?**
Flight attributes change occasionally. SCD Type 2 preserves history so historical price facts always join to the correct flight attributes for their time period.

**Why Dataproc Serverless?**
Batch job runs once daily, completes in 2-3 minutes. Serverless charges only for execution time — no idle cluster cost.

**Why Cloud Composer?**
Airflow provides dependency management, retry logic, branching, XCom for passing data between tasks, and a visual DAG graph. More robust than cron + shell scripts.

**Why both BigQuery AND Snowflake?**
BigQuery handles streaming processing and anomaly detection. Snowflake handles analytics serving with natural language queries via Cortex Analyst. Demonstrates multi-platform expertise for portfolio purposes.

**Why Snowflake uses simulated prices?**
AviationStack free tier provides schedule data only — no pricing data. Prices are simulated in both GCP (Function B, ±20% variance) and Snowflake (SQL UNIFORM() function). In production, BigQuery Gold would export to GCS and Snowpipe would load real prices into Snowflake.

**Why Dynamic Tables over scheduled tasks?**
Dynamic Tables auto-refresh when source data changes — no cron job, no Airflow task, no manual intervention. Snowflake handles the refresh dependency chain automatically.

**Why Semantic Views over YAML for Cortex Analyst?**
Snowflake deprecated the YAML file approach in favor of native SQL Semantic Views — better RBAC, governance, and tooling support. CREATE SEMANTIC VIEW is the current recommended approach.

